I did find one interesting thing. though.

771
00:51:49.606 --> 00:51:50.857
In of all places.

772
00:51:53.110 --> 00:51:54.111
coffee cup.

773
00:51:56.446 --> 00:51:56.780
RENTALS

774
00:51:57.030 --> 00:51:58.448
E.V.. display home work station.

775
00:52:00.951 --> 00:52:04.454
You spent four years
erasing Peter Parker from existence?

776
00:52:05.455 --> 00:52:08.041
No wonder the spider's
trying to swallow up t the man.

777
00:52:08.625 --> 00:52:10.544
I wonder if MJ would even recognize you.

778
00:52:11.628 --> 00:52:12.212
TUNE UPS

779
00:52:13.964 --> 00:52:15.465
I think I might go see how she's doing.

780
00:52:15.715 --> 00:52:16.716
I'm not gonna let that happen.

781
00:52:16.967 --> 00:52:20.887
No. her roommate was nice enough
to post a new address online.

782
00:52:21.138 --> 00:52:23.807
How about this? I'll race you there.

783
00:52:23.807 --> 00:52:24.141
BKES-P
RENTAL

784
00:52:24.558 --> 00:52:25.308
If you touch her.

785
00:52:25.976 --> 00:52:27.561
Better start swinging

786
00:52:27.727 --> 00:52:28.979
I'm fast.

787
00:52:52.335 --> 00:52:53.420
Hey.

788
00:52:53.587 --> 00:52:55.505
It's a long way to MJ's.

789
00:52:56.506 --> 00:52:58.008
You better pick up the pace.

790
00:53:05.098 --> 00:53:06.933
E.V.. track physical anomalies.

791
00:53:08.185 --> 00:53:11.021
Searching for physical anomalies
between subjects.

792
00:53:11.188 --> 00:53:12.272
Please stand by.

793
00:53:16.860 --> 00:53:19.279
hank you all so much for coming today

794
00:53:26.286 --> 00:53:27.454
I'm sorry about that.

795
00:53:27.621 --> 00:53:29.456
Give it up for Spider-Man.

796
00:53:29.706 --> 00:53:32.709
in a race for the love of his life.
and it's not looking good

797
00:53:35.212 --> 00:53:37.464
Come on. Spidey Keep up

798
00:53:38.632 --> 00:53:39.549
Excuse me. Sorry.

799
00:53:48.391 --> 00:53:49.392
Spider-Man!

800
00:53:53.063 --> 00:53:54.898
E.V.. run these numbers with the others.

801
00:53:58.151 --> 00:54:00.487
Analyzing jump distances for patterns.

802
00:54:02.906 --> 00:54:04.241
Get me that jump data.

803
00:54:04.658 --> 00:54:05.659
Calculating.

804
00:54:09.663 --> 00:54:11.164
Come on. I need an answer!

805
00:54:12.832 --> 00:54:14.334
Calculations complete.

806
00:54:29.933 --> 00:54:32.102
You have a limit
to your jump radius. don't ya?

807
00:54:32.686 --> 00:54:33.770
Thirty-three feet.

808
00:54:34.771 --> 00:54:37.023
I don'ts see anybody up here
for you to hop into.

809
00:54:38.441 --> 00:54:39.526
Very clever.

810
00:54:40.026 --> 00:54:43.113
Like I said. you're not getting near her.

811
00:54:58.878 --> 00:55:00.380
-Hey. hey. hey.
-MJ! I'm sorry. but you're in danger.

812
00:55:00.630 --> 00:55:01.464
-Where's your roommate?
-What?

813
00:55:01.631 --> 00:55:02.465
Where's Ned?

814
00:55:02.632 --> 00:55:03.800
In Boston with friends. Why?

815
00:55:03.967 --> 00:55:05.135
Okay. good. You gotta come with me.

816
00:55:05.385 --> 00:55:06.803
What? I don't know
if you're the real Spider-Man.

817
00:55:07.053 --> 00:55:08.555
-I'm not coming with you.
-We don't have time for this.

818
00:55:08.722 --> 00:55:10.807
-Please. Come on.
-You need to get out of my apartment.

819
00:55:10.974 --> 00:55:12.142
Look. this is gonna sound insane.

820
00:55:12.309 --> 00:55:14.728
but there is someone who is after you
who is really dangerous. okay?

821
00:55:14.894 --> 00:55:16.646
And I promised you
that I would keep you safe.

822
00:55:17.814 --> 00:55:19.733
Please. you just have to trust me. Come on.

823
00:55:23.153 --> 00:55:24.321
Fine.

824
00:55:30.994 --> 00:55:32.078
Web. Stop.

825
00:55:35.665 --> 00:55:36.666
Web. Stop.

826
00:55:40.754 --> 00:55:41.838
Web stop.

827
00:55:47.427 --> 00:55:48.678
-Are you okay?
-Yeah. yeah. I'm fine.

828
00:55:48.928 --> 00:55:51.264
Okay. We should be safe up here.

829
00:55:51.514 --> 00:55:52.515
Okay. well. safe from what?

830
00:55:53.933 --> 00:55:55.268
I'm not entirely sure.

831
00:55:55.435 --> 00:55:56.853
Okay. well. what do they want with me?

832
00:55:57.604 --> 00:55:59.272
-I don't know.
-You don't know?

833
00:56:00.023 --> 00:56:02.275
It doesn't make any sense.
Why would they choose me?

834
00:56:02.525 --> 00:56:04.778
I wish I could tell you. I just.

835
00:56:07.864 --> 00:56:09.449
We knew each other. didn't we?

836
00:56:13.119 --> 00:56:14.120
What?

837
00:56:15.121 --> 00:56:16.373
It's the only explanation.

838
00:56:17.791 --> 00:56:18.958
It's been driving me crazy for years

839
00:56:19.209 --> 00:56:21.544
all the times that Spider-Man
saved either me or Ned.

840
00:56:22.295 --> 00:56:23.296
It was the Washington Monument

841
00:56:23.463 --> 00:56:25.965
and then it was London and Prague
and the Night Monkey.

842
00:56:26.966 --> 00:56:29.302
I mean. twice is a coincidence.
but over and over again.

843
00:56:31.721 --> 00:56:33.390
We knew each other. Tell me I'm wrong.

844
00:56:35.475 --> 00:56:36.476
Well. you're wrong.

845
00:56:36.643 --> 00:56:39.396
What were we?
Were we classmates or friends or something?

846
00:56:40.063 --> 00:56:42.232
Look. I don't know what you're talking about.

847
00:56:42.482 --> 00:56:43.566
Were we something more?

848
00:56:45.819 --> 00:56:47.987
I just. I can't. I can't remember.

849
00:56:48.238 --> 00:56:50.156
And I feel like someone scrambled my brain.

850
00:56:50.323 --> 00:56:52.158
And you're the only one who would know why

851
00:56:53.326 --> 00:56:54.494
This is crazy. I can't.

852
00:56:54.661 --> 00:56:56.579
I know that you can't
tell me the truth.

853
00:56:59.582 --> 00:57:00.750
But I need to know.

854
00:57:05.922 --> 00:57:07.924
Maybe there's a part of me
that still remerbers.

855
00:57:48.631 --> 00:57:49.549
Peter.

856
00:57:51.551 --> 00:57:52.552
MJ.

857
00:57:52.719 --> 00:57:53.803
Hey. Peter.

858
00:58:00.310 --> 00:58:01.728
I've missed you so much.

859
00:58:06.733 --> 00:58:08.401
I can't believe you figured it out.

860
00:58:08.902 --> 00:58:09.903
I did.

861
00:58:15.658 --> 00:58:18.077
Go ahead. Peter. Touch her.

862
00:58:19.579 --> 00:58:20.830
Hold her.

863
00:58:22.248 --> 00:58:23.666
You've been wanting to for so long.

864
00:58:32.592 --> 00:58:34.177
True love's kiss breaks the spell.

865
00:58:35.094 --> 00:58:36.930
and reunites the star-crossed lovers.

866
00:58:39.182 --> 00:58:40.266
MJ would vomit.

867
00:58:43.102 --> 00:58:44.687
You really are a simple spider. aren't you?

868
00:58:48.274 --> 00:58:49.192
I see why you like her.

869
00:58:49.943 --> 00:58:50.944
She's..

870
00:58:52.111 --> 00:58:53.530
she's smart.

871
00:58:54.113 --> 00:58:55.114
funny

872
00:58:56.032 --> 00:58:57.283
and a little dark and twisted

873
00:59:01.371 --> 00:59:02.372
mean. it is sad.

874
00:59:03.540 --> 00:59:06.626
There is. like. no thoughts of you in here

875
00:59:08.044 --> 00:59:09.212
whatsoever.

876
00:59:10.797 --> 00:59:12.131
But you knew that. didn't you?

877
00:59:13.550 --> 00:59:14.801
You're a monster.

878
00:59:15.718 --> 00:59:17.387
If you loved someone
the way that I love her.

879
00:59:17.637 --> 00:59:20.306
then you'd know that
what you're doing right now is unforgivable.

880
00:59:20.557 --> 00:59:21.558
Is that so?

881
00:59:28.565 --> 00:59:31.568
You know. some people would kill
to hold the person they love one last time.

882
00:59:33.570 --> 00:59:34.904
Stop it now.

883
00:59:44.747 --> 00:59:46.082
You're running out of time. Peter.

884
00:59:47.250 --> 00:59:50.753
Soon enough. it won't just be your friends
who don't remember Peter Parker.

885
00:59:52.255 --> 00:59:53.923
Maybe you should write a letter to yourself

886
00:59:58.595 --> 00:59:59.596
Get out of her.

887
01:00:01.180 --> 01:00:02.515
Who's the monster now. Peter?

888
01:00:25.872 --> 01:00:26.873
MJ.

889
01:00:27.540 --> 01:00:29.709
MJ. No. no. no. Oh. God.

890
01:00:29.959 --> 01:00:31.461
Oh. God. please. no. come on.

891
01:00:31.628 --> 01:00:33.212
Come on. come on. come on.

892
01:00:33.379 --> 01:00:35.798
Oh. thank God. Oh. thank God.

893
01:00:36.049 --> 01:00:38.801
Oh. you're okay. Oh. you're okay.

894
01:00:39.052 --> 01:00:40.219
Oh. I'm so sorry.

895
01:00:42.722 --> 01:00:44.891
Stop. Wait. wait. stop. stop.
please. I'll quit.

896
01:00:45.058 --> 01:00:47.143
You win. you win. you win.
Just don't hurt her.

897
01:00:50.229 --> 01:00:51.648
You're a mess Spider-Man.

898
01:00:54.400 --> 01:00:55.818
Anytime I want.

899
01:00:55.985 --> 01:00:57.320
can be anyone I want.

900
01:00:58.571 --> 01:01:00.323
So you can't protect MJ.

901
01:01:01.741 --> 01:01:03.326
even from herself.

902
01:01:10.750 --> 01:01:12.085
It really is a nice letter.

903
01:01:13.086 --> 01:01:14.170
Little heavy-handed

904
01:01:14.420 --> 01:01:15.421
But not bad.

905
01:01:34.357 --> 01:01:36.859
You're okay.
I'm gonna take you someplace safe.

906
01:01:37.026 --> 01:01:38.027
What?

907
01:01:39.445 --> 01:01:40.530
Take me to 3165.

908
01:01:40.697 --> 01:01:41.864
Lafayette Street

909
01:01:42.031 --> 01:01:44.367
Navigating to Empire State University.

910
01:01:49.455 --> 01:01:50.707
Wait. wait. wait! Okay.

911
01:01:52.959 --> 01:01:53.960
-I got you. I got you.
-Are you sure?

912
01:01:54.210 --> 01:01:54.961
-Yep.
-Okay.

913
01:01:55.211 --> 01:01:56.212
'Cause I feel like
I'm slipping a little bit.

914
01:01:56.462 --> 01:01:57.380
-You're not slipping.
-Okay.

915
01:01:59.298 --> 01:02:00.466
You're okay. you're okay. you're okay.

916
01:02:00.633 --> 01:02:02.218
Yeah. yeah. yeah. I'm fine. I'm fine.

917
01:02:05.888 --> 01:02:06.556
Okay.

918
01:02:06.806 --> 01:02:07.890
Can we just slow down

919
01:02:08.057 --> 01:02:09.392
-for like two seconds. please?
-Well. we're almost there.

920
01:02:09.559 --> 01:02:11.644
Yeah. yeah. but you just told me
I was mind controlled.

921
01:02:11.894 --> 01:02:12.729
Well. not technically.

922
01:02:12.895 --> 01:02:13.980
I mean. you're lucky
I believe in that stuff. okay?

923
01:02:14.230 --> 01:02:16.232
Because governments have been doing it
for years. especially the French.

924
01:02:17.066 --> 01:02:18.067
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

925
01:02:18.317 --> 01:02:20.653
Look. Sorry. I'm just trying
to take you someplace safe. okay?

926
01:02:25.324 --> 01:02:26.576
I don't feel safe.

927
01:02:28.661 --> 01:02:29.495
Oh. shit.

928
01:02:34.667 --> 01:02:35.835
-Sorry.
-Oh. watch out!

929
01:02:45.428 --> 01:02:46.679
You're losing it. kid.

930
01:02:47.096 --> 01:02:49.515
Thought you'd be able to see that coming
a mile away.

931
01:02:49.682 --> 01:02:50.683
What is wrong with you?

932
01:02:50.850 --> 01:02:52.018
-You could've killed us.
-Excuse me.

933
01:02:52.518 --> 01:02:55.021
You show up to my house unannounced.
what do you think's gonna happen?

934
01:02:55.188 --> 01:02:56.022
Wait. this is your house?

935
01:02:56.189 --> 01:02:57.273
-No. no. Don't. don't. don't
-Who the hell is that?

936
01:02:57.690 --> 01:02:58.691
Who the hell are you?

937
01:02:59.358 --> 01:03:00.359
She's.

938
01:03:01.360 --> 01:03:02.361
You know.

939
01:03:02.528 --> 01:03:04.530
No. I don't know.
That's why I just asked you.

940
01:03:04.697 --> 01:03:07.366
She's in danger. Frank.
Look. I need your help. okay?

941
01:03:07.533 --> 01:03:09.535
-Yeah. looks like it.
-Well. come on. You owe me.

942
01:03:10.203 --> 01:03:12.538
-For... Aren't you sick of this story?
-Staten Island!

943
01:03:12.705 --> 01:03:14.040
Nah. Staten Island

944
01:03:14.290 --> 01:03:16.626
What more do you want me to do?
I literally saved your life.

945
01:03:16.793 --> 01:03:17.627
You're out of your mind. kid!

946
01:03:17.877 --> 01:03:18.711
What. I gotta save it twice

947
01:03:18.961 --> 01:03:20.046
-to get a favor out of you?
-That guy couldn't hit me.

948
01:03:20.213 --> 01:03:22.298
-with a handful of rice.
-I mean. what does that sound like to you?

949
01:03:22.548 --> 01:03:23.549
-I had him exactly where I want him
-A drug dealer was gonna shoot a guy

950
01:03:23.800 --> 01:03:24.884
-I'm seein' him right there.
... then I webbed the gun.

951
01:03:25.051 --> 01:03:26.219
.out of the drug dealer's hand
-I know exactly what I'm

952
01:03:26.385 --> 01:03:27.553
.completely up for.
..and then kicked that drug dealer.

953
01:03:27.720 --> 01:03:28.554
-Okay. fine. go ahead.
back into a storage container.

954
01:03:28.805 --> 01:03:30.139
-What would you call that?
-What does that sound like to you?

955
01:03:31.474 --> 01:03:32.558
I don't care. I just wanna go home.

956
01:03:33.559 --> 01:03:35.645
That's an excellent idea. Kick rocks

957
01:03:35.895 --> 01:03:37.480
-Go home.
-No. wait. wait. Frank. Frank. Frank. wait.

958
01:03:37.730 --> 01:03:38.564
Please.

959
01:03:39.732 --> 01:03:43.319
I have got to keep her safe. okay?
And I don't have anywhere else to go.

960
01:03:47.240 --> 01:03:48.241
You like chili?

961
01:03:49.575 --> 01:03:50.493
I made chill.

962
01:03:52.328 --> 01:03:53.246
All right. Just..

963
01:03:54.163 --> 01:03:55.248
watch out for the claymores.

964
01:03:55.498 --> 01:03:57.917
Don't wanna pick up pieces of you
for the next two weeks.

965
01:03:59.418 --> 01:04:01.420
Hey. I definitely would not eat that chili.

966
01:04:03.339 --> 01:04:05.007
So. you telling me that maniac.

967
01:04:05.258 --> 01:04:08.427
behind all that tank nonsense
is nothing but a goddamn teenager?

968
01:04:08.678 --> 01:04:12.265
And it's not just the tank. it's every attack
on Damage Control this past month.

969
01:04:12.515 --> 01:04:14.267
And how does a kid learn how to drive a tank'

970
01:04:14.517 --> 01:04:15.518
I don't know. Frank.

971
01:04:15.685 --> 01:04:18.688
-Beat you all over the street like that.
-She did not beat me.

972
01:04:19.689 --> 01:04:20.773
This your family?

973
01:04:23.776 --> 01:04:25.528
Would you get the hell away from that?

974
01:04:26.195 --> 01:04:28.364
Look. I got one rule in this house.

975
01:04:28.531 --> 01:04:31.117
You don't touch anything.
You don't move anything.

976
01:04:31.367 --> 01:04:34.287
You sure as shit don't ask me
any goddamn questions about anything.

977
01:05:13.826 --> 01:05:14.660
But she's classified as a telepath.
And now we have a name.

978
01:05:14.994 --> 01:05:18.164
DCACG

979
01:05:18.748 --> 01:05:19.749
"Jean Grey.

980
01:05:21.667 --> 01:05:25.254
Yeah. These are the Damage Control sites
that she hasn't hit yet.

981
01:05:25.504 --> 01:05:26.756
so if she surfaces.

982
01:05:27.006 --> 01:05:28.925
then my facial tracking program
will pick her up.

983
01:05:30.009 --> 01:05:30.927
Right.

984
01:05:31.177 --> 01:05:32.511
Oh. yeah? What then?

985
01:05:34.931 --> 01:05:37.516
Well. don't worry about "what then.
Just look after her.

986
01:05:37.767 --> 01:05:39.185
Don't worry about it. huh?

987
01:05:39.352 --> 01:05:41.187
I'm just supposed to sit here and
babysit your girlfriend?

988
01:05:41.354 --> 01:05:43.022
-I don't need to be babysat. so yeah.
-She's not my girlfriend.

989
01:05:43.189 --> 01:05:45.358
All right. all right.
Look. what's the plan. huh?

990
01:05:45.524 --> 01:05:48.945
Just gonna hope that
your facial tracking program works?

991
01:05:49.111 --> 01:05:51.197
And you get yourself killed.
I gotta watch her the rest of my life?

992
01:05:51.364 --> 01:05:53.699
I'm not gonna get killed. Frank.
I can catch her. okay?

993
01:05:53.866 --> 01:05:54.617
I just...

994
01:05:54.784 --> 01:05:57.370
I just have to fix my inhibitor
and then I'll be good to go.

995
01:05:57.870 --> 01:05:59.288
Well. what do you need to do that?

996
01:06:00.706 --> 01:06:04.293
Frank. You do not have
what I need to do that. okay?

997
01:06:05.795 --> 01:06:07.129
You know you've got some mouth on you.

998
01:06:07.296 --> 01:06:09.131
What do you think.
you have an anti-static mat.

999
01:06:09.298 --> 01:06:10.883
tonal probe. and micro tools?

1000
01:06:11.550 --> 01:06:12.969
got all that shit.

1001
01:06:13.552 --> 01:06:14.553
What for?

1002
01:06:14.720 --> 01:06:16.138
-Bombs.
-Bingo.

1003
01:06:18.557 --> 01:06:19.725
Unbelievable.

1004
01:06:31.487 --> 01:06:33.656
Hey. do you think it's safe
to maybe call someone

1005
01:06:33.823 --> 01:06:35.491
and let them know I'm okay?

1006
01:06:39.912 --> 01:06:40.913
Like your boyfriend?

1007
01:06:42.164 --> 01:06:44.500
No. Like my roommate

1008
01:06:48.504 --> 01:06:50.923
I don't think that's such a good idea.
you know. because

1009
01:06:52.008 --> 01:06:55.344
she already knows who he is.
and she can inhabit anyone she wants. so.

1010
01:06:55.511 --> 01:06:56.512
Right. Yeah.

1011
01:06:56.679 --> 01:06:58.014
Yeah. yeah. yeah. You're right.

1012
01:06:58.180 --> 01:07:00.683
-Sorry.
-No. it's fine. I totally get it.

1013
01:07:02.852 --> 01:07:04.103
If I called my boyfriend

1014
01:07:05.021 --> 01:07:07.189
he'd just ask me a bunch of questions
that I couldn't answer.

1015
01:07:07.356 --> 01:07:10.693
and then he'd tell me
I was being withholding again

1016
01:07:10.860 --> 01:07:12.695
-Withholding?
-Yep.

1017
01:07:12.862 --> 01:07:14.697
Sounds like your boyfriend's kind of a jerk.

1018
01:07:17.533 --> 01:07:18.617
But why'd he think you're withholding?

1019
01:07:19.618 --> 01:07:23.539
I don't know. You tell me.
masked vigilante behind the curtain.

